.Dd August 12, 2026
.Dt JG-BROWSE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jg-browse
.Nd open a webpage in a browser
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl acefios
.Op Fl U
.Op Fl w | v
.Op Ar url
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens a URL in a web browser,
headlessly if possible.
The subcommand complements
.Xr jg-serve 1
and is designed to be further controlled using
.Xr jg-ws 1 ,
although this aspect is a work-in-progress and should be considered unstable.
.Pp
If no
.Ar url
is specified on the command-line,
.Nm
defaults to the URL
.Dq Em http://localhost:1337/
for consistency with the
.Xr jg-serve 1
command.
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh OPTIONS
.\" Defines a string named $1 containing the English name of a numeral (0-10)
.de EngNum
.	ie        \\$2=0  .ds \\$1 zero
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=1  .ds \\$1 one
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=2  .ds \\$1 two
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=3  .ds \\$1 three
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=4  .ds \\$1 four
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=5  .ds \\$1 five
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=6  .ds \\$1 six
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=7  .ds \\$1 seven
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=8  .ds \\$1 eight
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=9  .ds \\$1 nine
.	el \{ .ie \\$2=10 .ds \\$1 ten
.	el \{             .ds \\$1 \\$2
.	\}\}\}\}\}\}\}\}\}\}\}
..
.
.\" Outputs a list of environment variables used to locate a browser
.de EnvList
.	if \\n(.$<1 .return
.	ie \\n(.$=1 \{\
If the
.Ev \\$1
environment variable is set and points to an existing file,
its value is used as the browser's location,
and no system directories will be searched.
.	\}
.	el \{\
.		EngNum EnvCount \\n(.$
.		ie \\n(.$=2 \
.			No If either of the Ev \\$1 No or Ev \\$2
.		el \{\
.			No If any of the
.			while (\\n(.$>1) \{\
.				Ev \\$1 ,
.				shift
.			\}
.			No or Ev \\$1
.		\}
environment variables are set,
the first of the \\*[EnvCount] which references an existing file \
is used instead of searching system application directories.
.	\}
..
.Ss Browser selection
.Bl -tag -width 6n
.It Fl a , -auto
Use whichever browser is available:
Chrome,
Firefox,
Safari,
Edge,
Opera,
or Internet Explorer
.Pq in that order .
This is the default behaviour.
.
.It Fl c , -chrome
Use Google Chrome or Chromium.
.EnvList CHROME_CANARY_BIN CHROME_BIN CHROMIUM_BIN
.
.It Fl e , -edge
Use Microsoft Edge.
No distinction is made between the current Chromium-based version \
and the one retroactively branded by Microsoft as
.Dq Edge\~Legacy
.Pq 2015\(en2020 .
.
.It Fl f , -firefox
Use Mozilla Firefox.
.EnvList FIREFOX_NIGHTLY_BIN FIREFOX_BIN FIREFOX_DEVELOPER_BIN FIREFOX_AURORA_BIN
.
.It Fl i , -ie
Use Internet Explorer
.Pq Windows only .
.
.It Fl o , -opera
Use Opera.
.EnvList OPERA_BIN
Like Edge,
no distinction is made between the older Presto-based version of Opera \
and the current version based on Chromium.
.
.It Fl s , -safari
Use Safari.
.EnvList SAFARI_BIN
.El
.
.Ss General options
.Bl -tag -width 6n
.It Fl U , -unstable
Include experimental or beta versions of browsers when searching.
These have higher precedence in the search than stable versions.
.
.It Fl v , -version
Print the version string of the located browser.
The combination of this flag and
.Fl -auto ,
while legal,
emits the version string without identifying the browser in question.
.
.It Fl w , -where
Print the location of the browser instead of launching it.
This option is mutally exclusive with
.Fl v .
.El
.
.\"=============================================================================
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width FIREFOX_DEVELOPER_BIN
.It Ev DEBUG
If non-empty,
enables the display of non-essential feedback about the command's current state.
.
.It Ev CHROME_BIN
Location of Google Chrome.
.
.It Ev CHROME_CANARY_BIN
Location of Google Chrome Canary,
the nightly build of the browser geared towards developers.
Only used when the
.Fl -unstable
flag is set.
.
.It Ev CHROMIUM_BIN
Location of Chromium.
This is distinct from Google Chrome in that it lacks the closed-source,
proprietary components included with the latter.
.
.It Ev FIREFOX_BIN
Location of Mozilla Firefox.
.
.It Ev FIREFOX_AURORA_BIN
Location of Firefox Aurora,
a now-discontinued build channel that was a
.Dq halfway point
between nightly builds and Firefox\~Beta.
Support for Aurora releases ended in April 2017.
.
.It Ev FIREFOX_DEVELOPER_BIN
Location of Firefox Developer Edition, a
.Dq specially-themed
version of Firefox\~Beta with different branding and build flags.
.
.It Ev FIREFOX_NIGHTLY_BIN
Location of Firefox Nightly,
a nightly build of the browser intended for early testing and bug-reporting.
Only used when the
.Fl -unstable
flag is set.
.
.It Ev OPERA_BIN
Location of Opera.
.
.It Ev SAFARI_BIN
Location of Safari.
.
.El
.
